{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 29, :comments ["<b>And you shall sanctify.</b> With the anointing oil." "<b>And the sense of whatever touches them.</b> We learn it from 'if a man carries holy flesh' (Haggai 2:12), according to the plain sense — that it is as it sounds: if holy flesh touches bread or stew or wine or oil or any food, it becomes holy; so too the altar of burnt offering, concerning which too it is written 'most holy.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:39:26.737327987Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}